Third-party material
--------------------

AutoEq — https://github.com/jaakkopasanen/AutoEq
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2018-2022 Jaakko Pasanen.
  JoseonPC embeds measured headphone frequency responses and target curves taken from
  AutoEq (`crates/joseon-headphones/src/embedded_curves.rs`). Most measurements were made
  by oratory1990. Full license text, file list and measurers: docs/third-party-autoeq.md.

Headphone sensitivity figures are facts cited from manufacturer data sheets. The
diffuse-field offset comes from Hammershøi & Møller (2008), DOI 10.3813/AAA.918014.
Sources: docs/third-party-sensitivity.md.

Rust crates: realfft, rustfft, num-complex and their dependencies (MIT or Apache-2.0),
serde, serde_json and their dependencies (MIT or Apache-2.0), wgpu and naga (MIT or Apache-2.0),
bytemuck (Zlib or MIT or Apache-2.0), ab_glyph (Apache-2.0), tiny-skia (BSD-3-Clause),
png (MIT or Apache-2.0), pollster (MIT or Apache-2.0). Each new dependency must have a
GPLv3-compatible license.

